The ring will be destroyed if its enchantment is less or equal to -5,
or if (enchantment > rn2(7))- so for positive enchantments, the
chance is (enchantment/7).

If the scroll is uncursed, you will get a 1 incrase,
if its blessed, you will get a +3 increase..

So at 0, you obviously want to- other than that, we do an expected
value calculation:

 current         expected uncursed   expected blessed
   1              (6/7) * 2 = 12/7    (6/7) * (2/3+3/3+4/3) = 18/7
   2              (5/7) * 3 = 15/7    (5/7) * (3/3+4/3+5/3) = 20/7
   3              (4/7) * 4 = 16/7    (4/7) * (4/3+5/3+6/3) = 20/7
   4              (3/7) * 5 = 15/7    (3/7) * (5/3+6/3+7/3) = 18/7 

So if you have an uncursed scroll, its only statistically worth
it if the ring is at +2- although marginally so.
If you have a blessed scroll, its worth it at +1 or +2, but not
after that.


